# `fluid::Quality`

The quantity transported, its sources and its reactions.

## Signature

```cpp
fluid::Quality
```

## What It Does

Describes what `transport` follows through the network.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `mode` | Constituent or Age. | Constituent |
| `initial` | The starting quality at every node, `[..., node]`; required for a constituent. Pipes and tanks start at the values implied by their end nodes. | required for a constituent |
| `source` | The quality held at a reservoir and of an injection (negative demand), `[..., node]`. | `initial` |
| `pipe_rate` | A first-order rate, 1/s, `[..., pipe]`: the quality changes as `c e^{k Δt}`, so a decay is negative. | undefined (none) |
| `tank_rate` | The same for each tank, `[..., tank]`. | undefined (none) |

## Returns

A value; validated by `transport`.

## Errors

A constituent without `initial`, negative or non-finite values, the wrong width, mixed precision, and source or reaction fields for `Age` are rejected.

## Interpretation and Use

A decay written with a positive sign is a growth rate and is accepted. Reactions are exact exponentials, not approximations of the derivative. Pumps and valves hold no water and cannot react.

